Unique "electronic gift certificates" to return gifts Setouchi City added with hometown tax payment: Sanyo Shimbun Digital|SANDIGI
Electronic gift certificate "e-town gift".
Make a payment by contacting the dedicated equipment
On the 27th, Setouchi City announced that it will add its own electronic gift certificate "e-town gift" to the return of the hometown tax payment.
It can be used by merchants in the city from November.
For the first time, it is said that it is a local government in the prefecture.
If you make a hometown tax payment and select an electronic gift certificate as a return gift, the equivalent of one-third of the donation amount will be sent to the designated smartphone.
At the time of product purchase, the screen of the gift certificate is indicated, and the store side contacts the stamp-type dedicated equipment and settles it.
You can't transfer or resell.
It usually takes a certain amount of time from application to arrival, but electronic gift certificates can be received instantly.
Tourists can use it easily.
In addition to the five Furusato tax payment portal sites, it will also be accepted on the city's two special sites.
There are currently thirteen participating stores, aiming for one hundred by the end of this fiscal year.
In June, the Ministry of Internal Affairs and Communications (MIC) established a new system to regulate local products by reducing the amount raised from return gifts to less than thirty percent of donations in order to prevent excessive competition among municipalities.
According to the city, "We plan to use merchants such as companies that deal with local products, within the scope of the guidelines."
Setouchi City's hometown tax payment for the 18th fiscal year is about JPY400 million.
