Driving in high heels is dangerous!
Young people's pedal misstep accident occurs frequently (Auto Messe Web) - Yahoo! News
Violations that violate the Road Traffic Act
Reports of accidents caused by incorrect operation, such as pedal missteps, are attracting attention, but it is a big mistake to think that it is only a problem for elderly drivers.
According to the number of wrong-to-pedal accidents by chronology, the highest number of accidents by age group was 1080 cases under the age of 24, surpassing 1032cases for those aged 75 and older.
Mistakes are never common among the elderly, and it is important to call attention to young people in the same way.
Would you like to take a sleek at your feet?
you're going to take safety?
There is no description of the gender ratio or cause in this data, but unlike the elderly, which is thought to come from the decline of the body such as driving skills and reflexes, young people may be inadvertently distracted by other things such as music and conversations, and mistakes due to walking clothes.
In particular, some women choose high heels, pumps, sandals, mules, and various shoes depending on the clothes of the day and drive them as they are.
Some people know that it is not suitable for driving, but it is troublesome to change clothes, but there are many people who do not think at all about the possibility that it will lead to the danger and drive without masure.
However, driving with high heels and sandals violates the Road Traffic Act.
The first is "Violation of safe driving duty" that stipulates "ensuring the operation of the steering wheel, brakes, and other operations reliably" and stipulating that "do not drive in a way that causes an accident and harms a person".
In addition, there is a sentence of "Violation of compliance with the Public Safety Commission" in which the driver must comply with the matters stipulated by the prefectural public safety committee. For example, in the Miyazaki Prefectural Road Traffic Law Enforcement Bylaw, there is a sentence in Article XII: "Do not wear shoes that may interfere with the operation, slippers, high heels, or other items that may interfere with driving operations, or do not drive a vehicle (excluding light vehicles).
In each prefecture, even if it is not specified as high heels, the purpose is to consider driving with "mountains that may interfere with driving operations" as a violation.
Why is driving in high heels dangerous?
It is obvious when considering the basics of pedal operation safely.
In order to operate the pedal safely, the heel of the foot is fixed to the floor first, the foot is placed perpendicular to the brake pedal, and when stepping on the accelerator pedal, tilt the toes to the right as a fulcrum.
At this time, regardless of the behavior of the car, it is important to fix it firmly so that the heel does not shake.
However, in high heels, the area where the heel is grounded to the floor is small, and it is constantly blurred, and because there is an angle throughout the foot at the height of the heel, the area of the foot to be grounded on the pedal is also small, and it is difficult to make fine adjustments.
It is believed that this leads to danger.
In addition, most cars have floor carpets, but in this material, the heels of high heels tend to get caught, and the heel is caught and the pedal can not step on at the time of sudden braking, or the high heel can be taken off due to the beat when the heel is caught, sandwiched in the back of the pedal, and you may not be able to step on it.
In addition, there are cases where the heel catches on the back of the pedal when stepping on the pedal and then returning it, and the accelerator pedal can no longer return.
TOYOTA to make Subaru an equity-method-affiliated affiliate Accelerate joint development of new AWD vehicles and 86/BRZ next-generation models (response) - Yahoo! News
Toyota Motor Corp. and SUBARU agreed on a new business capital alliance on September 27th.
Toyota will acquire additional Subaru shares and become an equity-method affiliate.
Since agreeing to a business alliance in 2005, the two companies have been working together, such as SUBARU contract production of Toyota vehicles, the supply of vehicles from Toyota to Subaru, and the joint development of the FR sports cars "86" and "BRZ".
In June of this year, it also agreed to work on the development of EV-only platforms and EV vehicles utilizing Subaru's AWD (all-wheel drive) technology and Toyota's electrification technology.
In the business capital alliance agreed this time, Toyota will acquire additional Subaru shares.
Currently, Toyota's Subaru shares have a voting rights ratio of 16.83%, but they will acquire them additionally until they reach 20%.
Subaru will be an affiliate of Toyota's equity method.
On the other hand, Subaru will acquire Toyota shares, which is equivalent to the amount (up to eight billion yen) equivalent to the amount required for the acquisition of Subaru shares.
The two companies developed and strengthened their cooperative relationships through business capital alliances.
Joint development of AWD models and 86/BRZ next models, expansion of the installation of THS (Toyota hybrid system) on Subaru vehicles, cooperation in the connected field, and technical cooperation in the autonomous driving field will be promoted.
For the third year in a row, the minimum number of refugees accepted in the U.S.|Shizuoka Shimbun Ats. Co., Ltd.
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The U.S. State Department on Tuesday announced plans to reduce the number of refugees from around the world to eighteen thousand.
The minimum number since 1980, when the Refugee Act was enacted, will be renewed for the third year in a row.
The Trump administration aims to appeal to conservatives with a strict migrant and refugee policy in view of next year’s presidential election.
It is inevitable that there will be criticism from human rights groups, etc., as there is a constant number of people who will be expelled from the country in various places.
The Obama administration set the upper limit for the 17th fiscal year to eleven thousand people, but the Trump administration, which was inaugurated in January, overturned it and reduced it to fifty thousand people.
Forty-five thousand in the 18th fiscal year and thirty-thousand in the 19th fiscal year.
