BITPoint, which leaked three billion yen worth of crypto assets, to resume service (Gentosha Gold Online) - Yahoo! News
In July of this year, the crypto asset exchange “BITPoint”, in which the equivalent of three billion yen, such as Bitcoin (BTC), was illegally leaked.
Bitpoint Japan Co., Ltd., the operator, announced on September 30th that it will resume the remittance service of crypto assets.
There seems to have been a certain perspective, including measures to prevent a recurrence.
In July of this year, BITPoint leaked Bitcoin and Ripple
Bitpoint Japan Co., Ltd., which operates the crypto asset exchange BITPoint, announced on the 27th that it plans to resume the service of sending (remittance) services for crypto assets around 1pm on Monday, September 30th.
In addition to dealing with customers who have been harmed and interacting with the FSA, there seems to have been a certain point, including measures to prevent a recurrence, such as a management management system, including security.
“While putting safety first, we will resume our services as soon as possible and make efforts to restore trust from our users.”
In July of this year, there was an exodus of three billion yen worth of crypto asset fraud, such as Bitcoin (BTC) and Ripple (XRP).
At a press conference after that, regarding the survival of the business, he said, “There is about three billion yen in cash and deposits even if compensation is deducted,” and “We aim to resume services as soon as possible based on the premise of top priority for user protection.”
This article was published on CoinPost on September 27th.
