On the evening of the 25th, the "Omachi Taromen Management Council" (Representative of Suzuyama Kensuke), which is made up at a shop that provides Omachi's famous noodles "Taromen", served "Taromen" at the town general welfare center Misato, which has become an evacuation center for people affected by torrential rains.
It was soul food, which has been loved since the Kijima coal mine, cheering up the people affected by the disaster.
“The only thing we can do is to make it and eat it.”
The four restaurants on Taromen's menu worked together to make ninety meals, accompanied by onigiri (rice balls) and transported them to evacuation centers.
Udon noodles with thin noodles were added to the beef bone soup with the effect of ginger, and plenty of ingredients such as pork (head) meat, shrimps, and vegetables were served.
Not only to those living in evacuation centers, but also to those who came to the bath established by the Self-Defense Forces, "Taste of Omachi" was provided.
"I've been a fan since I was young, but it's the first time I've eaten it in a year. It's the first time I've eaten in a year," said a 66-year-old who moved in about a year and said, "It's the first time I've eaten it. It's delicious. I want to go to the restaurant this time I want to go to the restaurant."
Vice President Kenichiro Fujise, who finished cooking, rushed in and said, “We will cooperate if there is anything we can do so that we can return to our daily lives as soon as possible.”
<One year after the Eastern Iburi Earthquake> Securing water even in the event of a blackout Installation of a "watering faucet" directly connected to the water duct Hakodate's condominium:Hokkaido Shimbun Doshin electronic version
Countermeasures are underway at condominiums in the city of Hakodate, where water was cut off due to a blackout due to a blackout due to last September's Eastern Iburi Earthquake.
According to the water supply and sewerage department of the city's Corporate Affairs Bureau, in the year after the earthquake, seven condominium buildings installed a "watering fuct" that can emit water even if there is a blackout.
There are about four hundred apartments in the city, including four-story condominiums and private communal houses that are watered in a "water tank type" that may be cut off in the event of a power outage, and the department is calling for consideration of countermeasures.
There are two main types of water supply for houses: "reception type", in which water is stored in a water tank in the basement or on the rooftop, etc., and "directly connected type" in which water supply is provided directly from the city's water distribution pipes to each house.
Even if the water supply pipe is not damaged, if the electric pump that draws water from the receiving tank to each house does not move due to a power outage, etc., the water supply will not be possible, and the water will be cut off.
Training in preparation for distress (Aomori Prefecture) (Aomori Broadcasting) - Yahoo! News
The training to search and rescue those in distress ahead of the autumn mushroom picking season was carried out in Shingo Village.
Sixty people participated in the training held at Heikozawa Forest Park in Shingo Village, including the police, firefighters, and the hunting association.
At the opening ceremony, Chief Tsukeda of the Gonohe Police Station said, "I want you to work closely in close cooperation and train."
Mr. Takahashi's declaration "We will start mountain training and rescue training from now on"
The training was carried out with the assumption that the man who went out to see the mushroom picking did not come home even at night.
The participants were divided into three groups and searched through the mountains, calling the names of the missing men.
In Shingo Village, a man in his 70s who went into the mountain to pick wild vegetables in June disappeared and was rescued with injuries the next day.
In the training, we found a man who was injured and checked the cooperation from the search to the rescue by putting it on a stretcher and preparing for the autumn mushroom picking season, which is prone to distress.
