Cherry shrimp in the process of growth PT, water depth 290m shooting such as Shizuoka City|SHIZUOKA SHIMBUN AT S
Sakura Shrimp born this year who succeeded in shooting in the deep sea of Suruga Bay = 11th, off the coast of Kamahara, Shimizu-ku, Shizuoka City (provided by "Yui Sakura Shrimp Project")
The "Yui Sakura Shrimp Project" of the Marine Industry Cluster Council by industry-academia-government groups such as Shizuoka City has recently succeeded in photographing cherry shrimp, which is believed to have been born during this year's spring-summer spawning season, on the seabed at a depth of 290m in Suruga Bay.
The video of the growth process is valuable, and the people involved say that they want to lead to the elucidation of the ecology of cherry shrimp, which has many mysteries.
The photo was taken near the seabed about one to five kilometres off the coast of Kamahara, Shimizu-ku, the same city.
I checked about three hundred of them for seventeen minutes.
During the day, the conventional knowledge that cherry shrimp in the deep sea "forms a certain number of herds on the bottom of the sea" has been reconfirmed.
The adult body is about 40mm long, and the individual that was reflected is about 23mm long.
The spawning season was determined by comparing it with seasonal data of caught cherry shrimp.
The detailed analysis will be requested by Fujitsu Software Technologies, which make up the team, and the Shizuoka College of Industrial Science and Technology.
Keisuke Mizuno, project leader, says, "I want to capture the living figure of individuals in the growth process, including young prawns."
