Mie Prefecture's three Shinkin Bank (Kuwana-Mie Shinkin Bank, Kitaise-Ueno Shinkin Bank, and Kihoku Shinkin Bank) announced on the 26th that it had decided to reduce the withdrawal limit by cash card in order to prevent the damage of special fraud.
For depositors over the age of seventy who hold cash cards of Kuwana Mie, Kitaise Ueno, and Kihoku, and have not traded more than a certain amount at ATMs for the past three years, the maximum amount that can be withdrawn in a day with a cash card will be half a million yen.
The Kuwana-Mie Shinkin Bank and the Kita-Ise-Ueno Shinkin Bank will be downgraded on October 1st, and the Kihoku Shinkin Bank will be downgraded from November 1st.
In the prefecture, there have been a number of special fraud cases in which cash cards and PINs have been defrauded by financial institutions, police officials, etc. at ATMs, and Shinkin Bank officials said, "We would like to protect the customer's important deposits as much as possible."
