Children's amusement facilities and Minaminumahara-ko, construction outline will be decided Yamagata City|Yamagata Shimbun
Yamagata City is planning to build social capital by utilizing private capital (PFI) methods, and the winning bidders of the children's play facility and the Minaminumahara elementary school building have been decided, and an explanation of the outline of the facility was given at the city council's standing committee held on the 26th.
An image of a children's amusement facility to be newly established in Kataya, Yamagata City
The children's amusement facility is scheduled to be built on the north side of Yamagata's Kuchu in the Katatani area.
The building is a one-story steel-framed building with a total floor area of about three thousand square meters.
There is a semi-subterranean gymnasium, a cafe, and a library corner.
In addition, it is equipped with universally designed playground equipment so that children with disabilities can play outdoors, and three hundred parking spaces will be secured.
On the 5th of this month, a review committee was held at the city hall, and the shelter group (Yamagata City), which is made up of thirteen companies, sold for three hundred and fifty million yen, including design, preparation for opening, and maintenance and operation for fifteen years.
It will begin design and construction from January next year, and is scheduled to open in March 2022.
Map of Minami-Numahara Elementary School
Minami-Numahara Elementary School is a large-scale school with more than nine hundred children.
It is scheduled to be built on the north side of the current school building in Iizawa City.
It is a three-story reinforced concrete building with a total floor area of about 8580m2.
The number of classrooms is thirty, including two pools, a steel-framed gymnasium, and an after-school children's club.
On the 6th of this month, the Ichimura Corporation Group (Yamagata City), which consists of eight companies, sold it for four hundred and twelve million yen, including the design, the dismantling of the old school building, and the maintenance and operation costs for fifteen years.
It went into design and construction in December, and is scheduled to be completed in October.
