Akutagawa's self-written manuscript before suicide to be released for the first time Debilitating and heartbreaking literature theory|Shizuoka Shimbun Ats. Co., Ltd.
Written manuscript by Ryunosuke Akutagawa, which will be released for the first time at the Tabata Bunji Village Memorial Museum
Writer Ryunosuke Akutagawa (1892-1927) obtained a self-written manuscript of "Sequent Literary, Too Literary" written by Junichiro Tanizaki in his last years of fighting literary theory, by the 27th by the Tabata Bunshimura Memorial Museum in Kita-ku, Tokyo.
It will be exhibited at the museum from October 1st.
The existence of essays has been known, such as that it was recorded in a complete collection, but it is said that this is the first time that a self-written manuscript will be released to the public
It seems that Akutagawa wrote it a few months before he committed suicide, and Takeshi Tanei, a researcher at the museum, said, "You can see that Akutagawa, who has weakened both physically and mentally, has faced serious literary challenges with heartbreaking determination."
A total of twelve two-hundred-word manuscript papers were published in the April issue of Bungeishunju.
Greta Toonberi: “Why do adults laugh and threaten children?”
Swedish environmental activist Greta Thunberg gave a speech on September 23rd at the United Nations Climate Action Summit held in New York.
While his speeches are attracting attention, there have been messages that insult Greta.
Greta Toonberi: “Why do adults laugh and threaten children?”
A political commentator said on an American TV show about Greta, "I'm mentally ill. It's being used by my parents and the international wist," and the TV station where he used it apologized.
Even in Japan on the Internet, there are a lot of messages about Greta, such as "It's used and it's pitiful" and "It's better to go to school," etc.
Meanwhile, Greta posted on Twitter on September 26th, “Why do adults spend their time laughing and threatening teenagers and children?”
“It comes up to as many lies and conspiracy theories as you can think of.”
Greta said, “Look, it’s started again. As you’ve noticed, people who hate me are as active as ever. They follow my looks, my clothes, my attitude, and where I’m different. They come up with as many lies and conspiracy theories as they can.”
He pointed out that adults don’t want to deal with climate and environmental crises, so they seem to sway the topic.
I honestly don’t understand why adults spend their time laughing and intimidating teenagers and their children.
You’ll be able to do something better at that time.
I think they feel threatened by us.
However, don’t spend your time paying any more attention to them.
The world is starting to awaken.
Change is coming.
Even if the adults don't like the change, they don't like it.
I'll see you on the street on Friday!
On the 20th of the previous Friday, there was a strike on climate change in New York and other parts of the world.
Greta had also called for it to take place on Friday the 27th.
