On the 26th, the Nagai City Elementary School Friendship Athletic Competition was held at Koyo Seiki Athlete Field Nagai (City Athletics Stadium) in the same city, and in some races, long-distance runners belonging to Nasu Construction (the same city), Joseph Onsaligo (27), from Kenya, served as a pace maker.
With a light run, we set a new record for the three tournaments.
Mr. Onsaligo pulled the children in a total of four races in the men's 1000m and women's 800m.
In the men's, first-ranked Tomoya-kun Koseki (6th-year-year-old Hirano Elementary School) scored three minutes four-second 38 seconds, and in the women's first-ranked runner-up, Ransei Shigama (Isazawa Elementary School 6th year) scored two minutes 34 seconds 17, and second-ranked Rin Asano (Nagai Elementary School 6th grader) marked 2min 35sec 73, respectively, surpassing the tournament's record.
Mr. Koseki said, "It was hard to keep up with the fast On-Saligo player, but I was able to put up with it," and Mr. Shikama said, "Mr. Onsaligo called for 'pace-up.'"
Onsaligo said, "It was good for the children to run. I was able to do the perfect job myself."
The tournament was organized by the Nagai City Elementary School Sports Promotion Association in order to deepen friendship among the city's 6th graders, and it was the 39th time.
