State-of-the-art art that takes you to a different world Okayama art exchange opens in the center of the city: Sanyo Shimbun Digital|SANDIGI
Three-thousand-thousand-thousand-year-old depicting the future of the film, the people who toured the classroom that became
On the 27th, the international art exhibition "Okayama Art Exchange 2019" (sponsored by the executive committee made by the city and prefecture) held every three years in the center of Okayama City opened.
According to the enigmatic title of "IF THE SNAKE: If the Snake," art fans from Japan and abroad are enjoying cutting-edge art created by eighteen artists from nine countries.
For the second time in sixteen years, French artist Pierre Hiugh has been invited as artistic directors to develop works that make use of Okayama's climate and local resources.
About forty videos and three-dimensional works will be shown at thirteen locations, such as former Uchiyamashita Elementary School (Marunouchi, Kita-ku, Okayama City) and Tenjinyama Bunka Plaza (the same Tenjin-cho).
Prior to the opening ceremony, an opening ceremony was held at the same small school, and about a hundred people, including those involved, attended.
Mr. Masao Omori, Mayor of the Executive Committee, and Mr. Yasuharu Ishikawa, General Producers of the Executive Committee, said, "There are all kinds of works that stimulate intellectual sensibilities and stimulate imagination and creativity. If it becomes an exhibition that attracts attention from the world, we will cut the tape.
Family members and out-of-school students who visited immediately looked at a snake-shaped robot in response to the sounds of the surroundings in the danger of the schoolyard, and toured the school building that transformed into the stage of a video work depicting the world three thousand years later.
I was enjoying the art that brought me back to the other world.
A 15-year-old high school student in Tokyo, who is traveling with his father, said, "The works that take advantage of the atmosphere of the old school building are interesting. It makes me imagine the time that flowed to this place."
Closed on Mondays until November 24th (or the following day if it is a national holiday).
Hong Kong, Umbrella movement rally in five years Tens of thousands, aiming for the general election|Shizuoka Shimbun Ats. Co., Ltd.
It has been five years since the Umbrella Movement occurred, people gathered at the rally venue = 28th, Hong Kong (joint)
HONG KONG (Reuters) - Tens of thousands of rallies were held in a park near the Hong Kong government headquarters building of the Admiralty, which had the largest base of demonstrators, on the 28th, five years after the outbreak of the Umbrella Movement called for the democratization of Hong Kong’s chief executive’s election.
Around the venue, some young people took up the main road and threw a flaming bottle at the government building.
As the protests stemming from the proposed amendments to the Fugitive Offenders Ordinance continued, the participants renewed their determination to fight until the realization of a "true general election" that could not be won at that time.
Protestrations, which began in earnest in June, marked more than the 79th day of the Umbrella Movement's 112th day, and the protesters' demands expanded to "five major demands" such as electoral system reforms.
Ibaraki Kokutai Opens on the 28th Today|Sports|Saga Shimbun News|Saga Shimbun LiVE
The 74th National Sports Festival "Ibiki Ibaraki Yume Kokutai" was held on the 28th at Kasamatsu Athletic Stadium in Hitachinaka City, Ibaraki Prefecture, and the 11-day heated competition will start until October 8th.
About four hundred people, including athletes and managers, participated in thirty-three competitions except for the pre-anniversary tournament, and challenged the strongmen of the whole country with the pride of their hometown.
Until two years ago, the prefecture had slumped to 43rd place for the third year in a row, but last year it came up to 33rd place.
Strengthening for the national sports tournament to be held in the prefecture in 2023 is also progressing, and this year's goal is the first half of the 20th place.
In the pre-season competition held by the 16th, Saga Women's High School of Rhythmic Gymnastics Boys and Women's Gymnastics, adult gymnasts and boys and women's and women's competed for the sixth place.
In each competition, I would like to aim to advance to the top by riding the flow.
At the general opening ceremony, eighty-three players, managers, and headquarters officers marched to the 40th entry, and rugby men's men's player Kugo Ishikawa (Saga Koko) served as the flagbearer.
On the first day, there will be three sports: wrestling, table tennis, and karate.
